        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: интервью",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "интервью (intervyú) — \"an interview\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Певица дала интервью газете. Pevítsa dalá intervyú gazéte. The singer gave an interview to a newspaper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter and indeclinable: в интервью (intervyú). Брать интервью (intervyú) у + genitive — to interview someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "интервью (intervyú) was borrowed from English interview (EtymDB), which comes from French entrevue \"a meeting\", from the reflexive verb entrevoir \"to see each other\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
